 {r}←StopTatinServer port;tatin;ind;process;folder;url;request;counter;maxTries
⍝ Stops the server `StartTatinServer` started on `port` and deletes its temporary folder.
⍝ With an empty `port` every server `StartTatinServer` started is stopped.
⍝ The server is asked to shut down. One that has not ended within `maxTries` half seconds is left
⍝ alone, session and folder, and so is its entry: call this again once that session is closed.
⍝ Returns the port when the server was stopped, otherwise ⍬.
 r←⍬
 tatin←##.##
 :If 0=⎕NC'∆SERVERS'
     ⎕←'No server is running' ⋄ →0
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢port
     ind←'Select the server(s) to be stopped' 1 1 ##.##.Client.CommTools.Select↓⍕∆SERVERS
     :If ¯1≡ind
     :OrIf 0∊≢ind
         :Return
     :EndIf
     StopTatinServer¨∆SERVERS[ind;1]
     :Return
 :Else
     port←⊃port
     ind←∆SERVERS[;1]⍳port
 :EndIf
 ('No server started by StartTatinServer runs on port ',⍕port)##.Assert ind≤≢∆SERVERS
 (process folder)←∆SERVERS[ind;2 3]
 url←'https://localhost:',(⍕port),'/'
 request←tatin.Client.R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/v1/shutdown'
 :Trap 0
     {}tatin.Client.SendAndReceive url request
 :Else
     ⍝ Not answering any more is fine: we are about to make sure that it is gone
 :EndTrap
 maxTries←20
 counter←0
 :While ~process.HasExited
 :AndIf maxTries>counter←counter+1
     ⎕DL 0.5
 :EndWhile
 :If process.HasExited
     {}tatin.FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce folder
     ∆SERVERS←((⍳≢∆SERVERS)≠ind)⌿∆SERVERS
     r←port
     ⎕←'Tatin server on port ',(⍕port),' stopped'
 :Else
⍝ Most likely it is suspended on an error: session and folder are what is needed to find out why
     ⎕←'Tatin server on port ',(⍕port),' did not end; see its session window. Its folder: ',folder
     ⎕←'Once you have closed that session, StopTatinServer ',(⍕port),' removes the folder'
 :EndIf
⍝Done
